- action(n3,...), action(n5,...), action(n11,...), action(n14,...), action(n19,...), action(n22,...): Decision checkpoints ("is the process model OK", "is the project accepted", etc.) are modeled as action nodes instead of edge guards, misrepresenting their semantic role.
- branch(b1,...) through branch(b6,...): All XOR branches lack guard(...) statements, failing to encode explicit source conditions like "If the process model is 'NOT OK'" and "If the project is accepted".
- defines(v1,...) through defines(v6,...): Variable ranges are all empty {}, failing to specify valid value domains required for decision evaluation.
- branch(b7, AND) and precedence(b7, n10): Incorrectly models "fix them in the next session and extend the process to levels 2 and 3" as a parallel/concurrent path; the source describes it as a sequential conditional step.
- precedence(n6, n9), precedence(n9, b7), precedence(b7, n10): Forces the issue-fixing step to occur only after double penalty assignment, misaligning with the source's standalone condition "If there are any issues...".
- action(n15,...) and action(n16,...): Identical labels split from b4 with no differing guards or source justification, hallucinating redundant process fragmentation.
- actor(a_default, "[i1, ..., e1, ..., b7]"): Assigns every node—including synchronization and routing elements—to a single participant, contradicting source directives to "assign roles in the team" and "perform work according to your assigned role".

